      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While mild swelling can be normal, feeling significantly warmer and tighter is a symptom that warrants professional evaluation, even if you're worried about calling. Over-the-counter medication and ice might help with general discomfort, but they don't rule out other issues like blood clots, which are a concern post-surgery. Given the localized warmth, it would be safest to call your surgeon's after-hours line or a nurse helpline before making a decision.",
